{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night","id":1444129,"title":"A Fortitude power to represent how stakes work in \"Fright Night\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-15T21:10:13-07:00","id":1444129,"title":"A Fortitude power to represent how stakes work in \"Fright Night\"","content":"In &quot;Fright Night&quot;, stakes paralyze rather slowly. Evil Ed takes over two minutes to &quot;die&quot;, and almost gets the stake out before he does. Later, Dandridge is staked and just yoinks the stake out, though he is straining in a way that suggest he has been weakened, considering his previous feats of strength. At the end of the movie, Evil Ed is revealed to have survived, presumably because Peter Vincent pulled the stake out.<br /> <br /> So to represent this, how about this for a Fortitude power: instead of immediately paralyzing you, a stake causes you to lose 1 point of strength per round. Only once your strength drops to zero are you paralyzed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-16-2021, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T21:33:19-07:00","id":1444131,"title":"","content":"Weirdly, my interpretation of that was Evil Ed was faking it because he'd knew his friend would kill him otherwise. He just is a really bad actor.<br /> <br /> Though its also possible that stakes just don't actually work in this setting and Dandridge is injured because, well, someone shoved a giant piece of wood into his chest.<br /> <br /> I always like those moments like in Lost Boys:<br /> <br /> &quot;Vampire weaknesses don't apply if you invite one in.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ohhhhhhh!&quot;<br /> <br /> But yes, that is a solid version of the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T09:27:04-07:00","id":1444215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1444131#post1444131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weirdly, my interpretation of that was Evil Ed was faking it because he'd knew his friend would kill him otherwise. He just is a really bad actor.<br /> <br /> Though its also possible that stakes just don't actually work in this setting and Dandridge is injured because, well, someone shoved a giant piece of wood into his chest.<br /> <br /> I always like those moments like in Lost Boys:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Vampire weaknesses don't apply if you invite one in.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Ohhhhhhh!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But yes, that is a solid version of the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely say different rules apply to the Dandrige vampires. I mean, he eats apples because Christopher Sarandon imagined there was a literal fruit bat in Jerry\u2019s ancestry, so...yeah \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> There used to be a Protean 8 power that let you expel stakes, but I think I like Cajun\u2019s idea better. Might even work as a high-cost Merit, sort of the opposite of a stake causing Final Death, but again, I like the Fortitude angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T12:56:09-07:00","id":1444247,"title":"","content":"Fortitude 4, Stake Resistance<br /> When staked through the heart, the vampire may make a rouse check to resist paralyses. The vampire nonetheless loses one point of strength per round. If the vampire has not managed to remove the stake before reaching 0 strength, they are paralyzed as normal.<br /> <br /> Some SI have taken to using stakes lined with several large metal barbs or hooks after witnessing this power in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-16-2021, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:08:56-07:00","id":1444296,"title":"","content":"Related thing that always bugged me: why can't you stack a vamp with a spear? After the head cuts a path, surely the haft would count? Same for arrows really ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T22:28:29-07:00","id":1444300,"title":"","content":"Uh, who says you can't? I've seen vampires staked with arrows in several movies. I can't think of someone using a spear on a vampire off the top of my head, but I've never seen someone try a spear, fail, and blame the failure on it being a spear instead of a stake. People improvising with any nearby source of pointy wood is kind of a staple of the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-17-2021, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T23:05:25-07:00","id":1444305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1444296#post1444296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related thing that always bugged me: why can't you stack a vamp with a spear? After the head cuts a path, surely the haft would count? Same for arrows really ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt comic Blade also made a very effective argument that a hardened wooden knife was better as a weapon than a stake.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/77/342911-48536-blade.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T23:57:56-07:00","id":1444308,"title":"","content":"The Tomb of Dracula comic also had Rachel Van Helsing use a crossbow to stake Dracula as well. So there's other precedent in comics.<br /> <br /> Of course, much depends on why you think staking works against vampires. It's an exercise not in logic, but magical thinking.<br /> <br /> In traditional vampire lore, it wasn't just any wooden stake. It was one made of a certain kind of wood that possessed the correct magical properties. Usually it was a stake made of either ash or hawthorn. But in certain regions, alternate wood was used. And sometimes it was an entirely different means of impalement like a large iron nail or spike. Iron, of course, also being know for its ability to protect people against malevolent supernatural creatures and magic.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the reason for impalement is linked to the belief that by piercing a bloated body, it would let out the blood the vampire had consumed. Of course, we know the reason why dead bodies bloat now is because of the release of bacterial gasses, not because the corpse is feeding on the blood of the living. But that's the magical reasoning behind it. There's also the thinking that by staking the body, you are pinning the dead to the ground so they can't rise. That implies not just piercing the heart, but using a particularly long stake that also plunges through the body into the ground. And in some places, staking wasn't done through the heart, but the head, stomach, or elsewhere.<br /> <br /> And sometimes it mattered how many times you hammered the stake into the heart.<br /> <br /> So depending on what inspires you, there are numerous ways you may want to interpret staking and how it works. You can make it both harder and easier depending on what you want to use, and even combine them. Maybe a normal wooden stake can get pulled as the OP stated, but one of ash or hawthorn works as normal per the rules, but if you do use to not just pierce the heart, but actually drive it into the ground, the vampire is completely destroyed. Maybe the material of the impalement device needs to be magical and solely made of that one item without any other material &quot;polluting&quot; it and disappointing its magical properties. Or maybe any sharp thing will work as long as the heart is pierced. Folklore and legend are not consistent, but the game rules need to be. It's just a matter of what combination works for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T04:46:37-07:00","id":1444324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1444305#post1444305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always felt comic Blade also made a very effective argument that a hardened wooden knife was better as a weapon than a stake.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/77/342911-48536-blade.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ha! Wooden knives don't work that well, for anything really, sadly, you can't take a shape made in metal, make it in wood, and expect the same results..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T12:40:25-07:00","id":1444533,"title":"","content":"Back on topic: yay or nay to Stake Resistance? Is it OP? UP? Needs a detail changed?<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Fortitude 4, Stake Resistance<br /> When staked through the heart, the vampire may make a rouse check to resist paralyses. The vampire nonetheless loses one point of strength per round. If the vampire has not managed to remove the stake before reaching 0 strength, they are paralyzed as normal.<br /> <br /> Some SI have taken to using stakes lined with several large metal barbs or hooks after witnessing this power in action. &quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T12:54:44-07:00","id":1444536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1444308#post1444308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tomb of Dracula comic also had Rachel Van Helsing use a crossbow to stake Dracula as well. So there's other precedent in comics.<br /> <br /> Of course, much depends on why you think staking works against vampires. It's an exercise not in logic, but magical thinking.<br /> <br /> In traditional vampire lore, it wasn't just any wooden stake. It was one made of a certain kind of wood that possessed the correct magical properties. Usually it was a stake made of either ash or hawthorn. But in certain regions, alternate wood was used. And sometimes it was an entirely different means of impalement like a large iron nail or spike. Iron, of course, also being know for its ability to protect people against malevolent supernatural creatures and magic.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the reason for impalement is linked to the belief that by piercing a bloated body, it would let out the blood the vampire had consumed. Of course, we know the reason why dead bodies bloat now is because of the release of bacterial gasses, not because the corpse is feeding on the blood of the living. But that's the magical reasoning behind it. There's also the thinking that by staking the body, you are pinning the dead to the ground so they can't rise. That implies not just piercing the heart, but using a particularly long stake that also plunges through the body into the ground. And in some places, staking wasn't done through the heart, but the head, stomach, or elsewhere.<br /> <br /> And sometimes it mattered how many times you hammered the stake into the heart.<br /> <br /> So depending on what inspires you, there are numerous ways you may want to interpret staking and how it works. You can make it both harder and easier depending on what you want to use, and even combine them. Maybe a normal wooden stake can get pulled as the OP stated, but one of ash or hawthorn works as normal per the rules, but if you do use to not just pierce the heart, but actually drive it into the ground, the vampire is completely destroyed. Maybe the material of the impalement device needs to be magical and solely made of that one item without any other material &quot;polluting&quot; it and disappointing its magical properties. Or maybe any sharp thing will work as long as the heart is pierced. Folklore and legend are not consistent, but the game rules need to be. It's just a matter of what combination works for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favourite interpretation is that Blood is the &quot;source&quot; of a Vampire's power, and the Heart is the &quot;core&quot; of our circulatory system; &quot;disrupting&quot; the system by piercing the &quot;core&quot; (without fully destroying it, which would be Final Death, in VtM terms) basically stuns the Vampire until it can regenerate the damage, which can't be done as long as the Heart is still pierced by something. But by that logic, anything piercing the Heart can do the job. Probably a Hellsing influence. Definitely doesn't work in VtM, where the object in question must explicitly be wood. So there seems to be something &quot;magical&quot; going on, but broader than the very specific categories of wood that were believed to have spiritual powers in Medieval Europe.<br /> <br /> Regarding the power itself: not a V5 player, so I don't have a great idea of the balance of things, but it doesn't seem out of place based on what else is listed on the wiki. I would maybe consider replacing Strength with Stamina (or whatever else if V5 doesn't use that any more). I get where you're coming from, with the idea of getting weaker the longer it is in, but since it's a Fortitude power it seems more appropriate, and the idea that you're running out of &quot;endurance&quot; to keep fighting back seems just as appropriate as running out of &quot;strength.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T13:07:39-07:00","id":1444537,"title":"","content":"Of course it is amusing when you consider that the entire lore about using stakes on vampires comes from the concept that you were nailing the vampire into their grave so they wouldn't rise. Both metal and wood were used historically. The idea of &quot;staking&quot; while outside of a coffin/grave a mostly modern idea.<br /> <br /> But with that in mind you could make a passive power that grants immunity to stakes while awake, but leaves you more vulnerable during the day. Basically staking the body to the ground regardless if it is through the heart or not still paralyzes the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:29:33-07:00","id":1444549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1444536#post1444536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Regarding the power itself: not a V5 player, so I don't have a great idea of the balance of things, but it doesn't seem out of place based on what else is listed on the wiki. I would maybe consider replacing Strength with Stamina (or whatever else if V5 doesn't use that any more). I get where you're coming from, with the idea of getting weaker the longer it is in, but since it's a Fortitude power it seems more appropriate, and the idea that you're running out of &quot;endurance&quot; to keep fighting back seems just as appropriate as running out of &quot;strength.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with Stamina is it doesn't represent his increasing difficulty pulling the stake out. He begins fully impaled, with the stake completely through his body and nearly a foot out his back. He manages to pull it most of the way out very quickly, but then can only pull it out further at a progressively slower pace, completely running out of strength with maybe four inches left in his chest.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T15:49:40-07:00","id":1444558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1444549#post1444549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only problem with Stamina is it doesn't represent his increasing difficulty pulling the stake out. He begins fully impaled, with the stake completely through his body and nearly a foot out his back. He manages to pull it most of the way out very quickly, but then can only pull it out further at a progressively slower pace, completely running out of strength with maybe four inches left in his chest.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I get where you're coming from. One idea that occurred to me was having Strength and Stamina both drain, another that increasing penalties could be applied over time. But I get that's just throwing in extra complications for the sake of a theme when just having Strength be the stat that goes down is a lot more convenient mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T18:29:47-07:00","id":1444578,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there some combo in the venture revised clanbook that let you slowly push out a stake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T19:26:05-07:00","id":1444745,"title":"","content":"This isn't to push the stake out after being paralyzed. This is a very short window to yank it out before you become paralyzed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:19:51-07:00","id":1445169,"title":"","content":"Added it to the Homebrew site: <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Stake_Resistance\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Stake_Resistance</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T13:08:55-07:00","id":1447617,"title":"","content":"Edited it to include rules for ripping the stake out of your chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T08:09:06-07:00","id":1447819,"title":"","content":"Should I keep the rouse check, or just have it be a pure passive?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Stake_Resistance\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/mw/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Stake_Resistance\" target=\"_blank\"> Stake Resistance - V5 Homebrew Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Stake_Resistance\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Stake_Resistance </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T11:22:52-07:00","id":1447832,"title":"","content":"Make it free, I think. It's level 4 and isn't that powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T23:48:12-07:00","id":1448102,"title":"","content":"In earlier editions, removing a stake from your own heart was something that could be done only by truly mighty elders, either fortitude 7 or protean 8. I don't know how it's done in v5, regardless I do like your idea about losing strength every round it's in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T04:51:47-07:00","id":1448116,"title":"","content":"There's no time limit on those older powers. This is, at most, five rounds before you are paralyzed normally. It's really a very different power, designed to mimic something specific from fiction.<br /> <br /> Really, I don't like those older powers specifically because they DON'T mimic anything from fiction. Really, in what movie or novel can a vampire slowly will the stake out over an unlimited amount of time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T19:28:29-07:00","id":1448187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1448116#post1448116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no time limit on those older powers. This is, at most, five rounds before you are paralyzed normally. It's really a very different power, designed to mimic something specific from fiction.<br /> <br /> Really, I don't like those older powers specifically because they DON'T mimic anything from fiction. Really, in what movie or novel can a vampire slowly will the stake out over an unlimited amount of time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair, VTM does have a much higher power ceiling for vampires than most other vampire fiction, especially western fiction. Part of it's appeal if you ask me. If there was a vampire movie or tv series out there that really gave me the feel of the WoD, I'd be all over it. And no, Kindred: the Embraced doesn't count <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T12:11:41-07:00","id":1448251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1448187#post1448187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well to be fair, VTM does have a much higher power ceiling for vampires than most other vampire fiction, especially western fiction. Part of it's appeal if you ask me. If there was a vampire movie or tv series out there that really gave me the feel of the WoD, I'd be all over it. And no, Kindred: the Embraced doesn't count <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it. Vampires in fiction are often much more powerful than WoD vamps. First off, fictional vamps can use their powers with a routineness that suggests that blood points and rouse checks are not a thing. They just...do things. They need blood, but they don't seem to burn that blood up using their powers routinely. They also get a bunch of powers right off the bat that requires a tremendous amount of XP for a WoD vampire. Lucy has the equivalent of Mistform and Presence within days of turning in the original Dracula, for example. Evil Ed has high levels of Protean within hours of turning. Jerry Dandrige constantly shapeshifts and displays zero hunger for doing so. Fictional vampires seem to just automatically get a strength of 6 or 7 or so rather than needing to develop a discipline or spend blood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T12:56:35-07:00","id":1448256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444129-a-fortitude-power-to-represent-how-stakes-work-in-fright-night?p=1448251#post1448251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see it. Vampires in fiction are often much more powerful than WoD vamps. First off, fictional vamps can use their powers with a routineness that suggests that blood points and rouse checks are not a thing. They just...do things. They need blood, but they don't seem to burn that blood up using their powers routinely. They also get a bunch of powers right off the bat that requires a tremendous amount of XP for a WoD vampire. Lucy has the equivalent of Mistform and Presence within days of turning in the original Dracula, for example. Evil Ed has high levels of Protean within hours of turning. Jerry Dandrige constantly shapeshifts and displays zero hunger for doing so. Fictional vampires seem to just automatically get a strength of 6 or 7 or so rather than needing to develop a discipline or spend blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I say power ceiling. I haven't watched Fright Night (I know, I'm a sinner), but from what I've seen of other vampire movies and series, the power level is generally underwhelming. Like 'The Strain' for instance, all it took to kill off the progenitor vampires was a piddly tactical nuke. Many types of vampires can beat the average run of the mill kindred right off the bat, but few settings have vampires that can, say, send dreams and nightmares to the entire world, or become completely indestructable, or fuse with the earth and move around continents. WoD vampires can also learn many more powers than what they were given at Embrace, unlike most fictional vampires that only have their own specific set of powers and nothing else.<br /> <br /> Besides, Kindred can get pretty powerful pretty fast in the WoD if they have powerful blood and a good mentor. Just look at Sergei Voshkov.<br /> <br /> To be honest with you, I don't really see why all the powers VTM vamps have must be taken from other pieces of fiction to be compelling. For me, VTM is the source of most of my 'vampire lore', and I feel they do it much more creatively and innovatively than other vampire franchises out there, to the point where other franchises have actually borrowed a lot from VTM. Until V5 anyway, which I feel was made to nerf the setting, but I guess we have the V5 debate thread for that.<br /> <br /> And coming back to the stake in the heart thing, most fictional vampires just outright die from being staked, like Dracula in most protrayals, let alone pull them out (or blast them out of their bodies) on their own with no time limit like some Elders can canonically do in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","user":"NuclearSnake","date":". 05-11-2021, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}